{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the degraded service and submitted the mitigation (accepted at stage `mitigation`).\n\n**Root cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. With that setting, traffic only reaches endpoints on the caller's node. The `recommendation` pod runs on `kind-worker`, while `frontend-proxy` runs on `kind-worker2`, so requests from the proxy were dropped. `/api/recommendations` hung until timeout.\n\n**Fix:** Patched the Service to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster` in `astronomy-shop`.\n\n**Verification:** `/api/recommendations` went from timing out to 200 in about 25ms. `/api/products` remained fast.\n\n**Other observations (not changed):**\n- The `otel-collector` Service also uses `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. It's not user-facing, and the collector runs an agent on every worker, so I left it alone.\n- `frontend` and `recommendation` have node selectors pinning them to specific workers. This isn't causing errors, so I left it as is."}}
